  "question": {
    "en": "Many individuals use an over-the-counter medication at some point during pregnancy. Examples include antacids (tums, maalox), allergy medications (Claritin), cold, sinus or flu (Mucinex, Sinex), cough medicines (Robitussin), anti-diarrhea (Imodium), laxatives (Metamucil), stool softener (Colace), gas relief (gas-X), anti-nausea (Dramamine), sleep agents (Tylenol PM), and pain medications (Advil, Aleve). Since we last met did you take any other over the counter medications before the end of your pregnancy?"
